(\(a\) Electricity consumption charges as per actual sub-meter reading at prevailing PSPCL/Electricity Department rates.) Tj T*
(\(b\) Fixed municipal water and sewerage maintenance charges of Rs. 500/- per month.) Tj T*
(\(c\) Personal broadband internet, DTH, and LPG cylinder expenses.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7. REPAIRS & MAINTENANCE:) Tj T*
(\(a\) Day-to-day minor repairs costing up to Rs. 1,500/- per occurrence \(including bulb replacements, tap washer leaks, minor fuse repairs\) shall be borne exclusively by the Tenant.) Tj T*
(\(b\) Major structural maintenance \(seepage, main electrical panel failure, building exterior repairs\) shall be attended to by the Landlord upon written notice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8. PROHIBITED USES & CODE OF CONDUCT:) Tj T*
(\(a\) The premises shall be used exclusively for private residential dwelling. Commercial, industrial, or illegal activities are strictly forbidden.) Tj T*
(\(b\) The Tenant shall not sublet, assign, mortgage, or part with possession of any portion of the premises to any third party.) Tj T*
(\(c\) Nuisance, offensive trades, or storage of hazardous, inflammable, or explosive materials is strictly prohibited.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(9. LANDLORD'S RIGHT OF ENTRY & INSPECTION:) Tj T*
(The Landlord or his authorized representative reserves the right to inspect the condition of the premises by providing 24 \(twenty-four\) hours' prior notice \(oral or via messaging\), except in situations of fire, pipe bursts, or emergency where immediate entry is necessary.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(10. JURISDICTION & DISPUTE RESOLUTION:) Tj T*
(In the event of any dispute or difference arising out of or in connection with this agreement, the parties shall endeavor to resolve it amicably. Unresolved disputes shall be referred to arbitration in accordance with the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996, and the courts at Chandigarh / Mohali shall have exclusive jurisdiction.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
